- `action(n1, "Start Screening Process")`: Hallucinates an initialization step; the source text explicitly states the process "begins by reviewing the support request" without any prior action.
- `action(n4, "End of Screening Process")`: Hallucinates a concluding step; the source text states the process "comes to an end" immediately after they "have communicated with the customer", meaning `n3` should connect directly to `end(e1)`.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Misassigns responsibilities; the text specifies "screening staff" perform the tasks, but the model assigns all nodes to a generic "Default" actor.
- `precedence(i1, n1)` through `precedence(n4, e1)`: Disrupts documented chronology by forcing control flow through undocumented start/end wrappers, breaking the direct sequential progression described in the text.